  "body": "Follow-up from the currency control plane design (#2062), §4 and §10 of\n`doc/2026-10-29T12-42-21Z_design_currency_control_plane/`.\n\n**This is a proof of concept, not the permanent currency service.** It makes its own decisions where the design is silent and must be reviewed before anything permanent is built on it.\n\n## Scope\n\nEnd-to-end, single currency, against the design's interfaces:\n\n- Registry (F1) + factory (F2) + gateway envelope (F3).\n- `register_currency` → `issue` 100 → `transfer` 40, with a signed graph object per event and a signed receipt returned.\n- One constrained holder account rejecting an overdraft at the cluster.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The full issue→transfer flow runs against a local TigerBeetle cluster, with `user_data_128` resolving to a graph object for each write.\n- An overdraft is rejected by the cluster, not by a check-then-write in the gateway.\n- A short write-up names every place the PoC guessed, so the review round has something to chew on.\n\n## Depends on\n\nF1, F2, F3.\n\n**Gate satisfied:** this is the PoC gated on \"do not start until the #2062 control-plane design fixes the gateway's registry/account-factory shape\" (#2298); #2062 now supplies that shape.\n\nRefs #2062, #2298\n",
